# Shell scripts keep LF whatever the host does.
#
# Git for Windows checks files out with CRLF by default. A shell script that
# reaches a Linux container or the deployment VM that way fails on its first
# line: dash reads `set -e` as `set -e\r` and reports "set: Illegal option -".
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else read by a shell or a Linux daemon.
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.Caddyfile text eol=lf
Caddyfile   text eol=lf
